#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069655} :activity/id #uuid "75b8321b-47ce-5d18-b03b-4a28719bcaba" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049428 :topic/id #uuid "f43e72f0-fa84-5dbe-8759-121893434566" :topic/math-academy-id 468} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069655 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069970 :tutorial/content "A **quadratic inequality** is an inequality that involves a quadratic expression. We can often solve quadratic inequalities using a graphical method.\n\nFor example, suppose we want to find the solution to the quadratic inequality \n\n$$\nx^2+2x-3 \\geq 0.\n$$\n\nLet's consider the graph of the corresponding parabola $y=x^2+2x-3,$ shown below.\n\n![](images/c0/c04ccf6db68a0e37663fecda4c2fb68ce12dc2a02821af45a6dcad73deeb7bc3.png)\n\nOur inequality is a \"*greater than or equal to*\" inequality. Therefore, we need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola is *above* the $x$-axis or *touches* this axis\n\nUsing the graph above, we notice that our parabola has roots at $x=-3$ and $x=1.$ The parabola is above the $x$-axis to the left of $x=-3$ and the right of $x=1,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/2d/2d1574ed8172f5b307e080c86b712a5e2d3a206dee0d74a797f692e9e9ae8731.png)\n\nTherefore $y = x^2+2x-3 \\geq 0$ when\n\n$$\nx \\leq -3 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad x \\geq 1,\n$$\n\nwhich is our solution.\n\n**Important:** Since we have a \"greater than *or equal to*\" inequality, the roots of the parabola are *included* in the solution set." :tutorial/id #uuid "7acbb382-158e-505a-a4fe-5598239a21dd" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3343 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "b8c84c90-fff3-5ec0-8816-e41fb5b44431" :step/math-academy-id 18527 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069656}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069656 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068751 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068585 :question/id #uuid "659cb2ef-191b-54f0-b0b5-d872cfd781bc" :question/math-academy-id "e-5061"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5dff5b7c-544a-5fda-a175-51ce4723a135" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049795} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049919}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069177} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069178} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233219} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233485} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250382} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302159} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302253} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345148}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving a \"Greater Than or Equal To\" Inequality Given the Graph of the Corresponding Parabola"} :step/id #uuid "7efd913e-aaa5-5399-80ff-5b2b175349ec" :step/math-academy-id 18528 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069760}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069758 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068823 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068673 :question/id #uuid "b75cf4ed-e93b-589c-88ed-1a277273945c" :question/math-academy-id "e-9935"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3eec195c-6549-5de2-b3f0-0417e5f518e7" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069176} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069230} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233703} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233837} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250378} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250383} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250385} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275150} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292703}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving a \"Greater Than\" Inequality Given the Graph of the Corresponding Parabola"} :step/id #uuid "6df23a8b-1690-5d8c-8f65-086b0c58b4a4" :step/math-academy-id 37410} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069759 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069994 :tutorial/content "Suppose we want to find the solution to the quadratic inequality\n\n$$\nx^2+x-6 <  0.\n$$\n\nWe first plot the graph of the corresponding parabola $y=x^2+x-6,$ shown below.\n\n![](images/c3/c30f81cbbe79d6b54f63070c5ea161fc94488413f893a80c3e451ed6a042b187.png)\n\nNotice that our inequality is a \"*less than*\" ($<$) inequality. Therefore, we need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola is *below* the $x$-axis.\n\nThe graph above shows that our parabola has roots at $x=-3$ and $x=2.$ Moreover, the parabola lies below the $x$-axis for all values of $x$ that lie between $x=-3$ and  $x=2.$ \n\n![](images/bd/bdef6fd120108576e48a4ac495abab327dc5e9c3bbe26d007724285a9d7d84a1.png)\n\nTherefore, $x^2+x-6 <0$ when\n\n$$\n-3 < x < 2,\n$$\n\nwhich is our solution.\n\n**Important:** Since our inequality is a \"*less than*\" inequality, the roots of the parabola are *not* included in the solution set." :tutorial/id #uuid "772a47c1-c2f0-54ee-a7c4-61d24a65bb87" :tutorial/math-academy-id 6197 :tutorial/title "Strict Inequalities"} :step/id #uuid "cc9b98d3-5b55-5a89-969d-d72ba706ab6b" :step/math-academy-id 37567 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069761}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069760 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068824 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068674 :question/id #uuid "58407228-e1f1-5d75-8786-a604caea671a" :question/math-academy-id "e-9975"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "36d4bf37-4818-58ac-9e39-75ce8ceef06a" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069054} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069179} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233449} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233830} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272203} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275120} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302264} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302294} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302295}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving a \"Less Than or Equal To\" Inequality Given the Graph of the Corresponding Parabola"} :step/id #uuid "f6eaab57-6262-53e0-95b6-d71e2ca519b4" :step/math-academy-id 37568 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069759}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069761 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068825 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068675 :question/id #uuid "f84c11bc-b14f-5285-a782-2130d31f9e49" :question/math-academy-id "e-9976"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc419917-fe34-5bf9-8bf0-1b022fce11ff" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069026} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069055} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233498} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233836} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275121} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275149} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302258} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302301} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400916}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving a \"Less Than\" Inequality Given the Graph of the Corresponding Parabola"} :step/id #uuid "d197c412-e6cd-5343-90ad-50aa69c262b0" :step/math-academy-id 37569 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069758}}] :activity/title "Solving Quadratic Inequalities From Graphs" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186068993}]}
